HOW TO RUN:

1. Open folder with VSCode
2. Install Flask extension
3. Run Main.py
4. You should see something like the following:
 * Serving Flask app 'main'
 * Debug mode: on
WARNING: This is a development server. Do not use it in a production deployment. Use a production WSGI server instead.
 * Running on all addresses (0.0.0.0)
 * Running on [PASTE THIS INTO YOUR BROWSER]
 * Running on [PASTE THIS AS YOUR URL IN HEALTH AUTO EXPORT]
Press CTRL+C to quit
 * Restarting with stat
 * Debugger is active!
 * Debugger PIN: [debugger pin]
5. Open your browser
6. Paste the url given on the second "*" under "WARNING..."

HOW TO EXPORT HEALTH DATA
1. Install Health Auto Export from App Store
2. Go to -> Automated -> New Automation
3. Set Automation Type to REST API
4. Get your IPv4 Address (See next guide below)
5. Set your URL to -> http://[YOUR IPv4 ADDRESS]:5000/data
6. Set Data Type to Health Metrics
7. In Select Metrics, select -> Sleep Analysis and Step Count
8. Set Export Format to JSON
9. Select Manual Export
10. Choose the days you would like to export data from
11. Select Begin export

HOW TO GET YOUR IPv4 ADDRESS/URL:
Easy way:
1. Run main.py
2. Locate the THIRD "*" under "WARNING: This is..." on the terminal
3. See that it says "Running on [PASTE THIS AS YOUR URL IN AUTO EXPORT]"
Hard way:
1. Open windows powershell and run: "ipconfig"
2. Look for IPv4 Address under your active WiFi adapter
3. Copy the IPv4 Address to your clipboard

NOTE:
* Health Auto Export cannot export screen time data. As of now, you must enter it manually in the web app
* If you do not have sleep data for an exported day, it will default to 0; to change that, add sleep data in your iphone Health app or enter it in the website